# L1 / B010 — security-scan (+layers), swagger, template-maintenance, verify, repository files, CLAUDE.md.

C R210 OL WF-020 | MUST | Security review reports concrete risks in the context of actual exposure, distinguishes confirmed findings from items needing verification (NEEDS VERIFICATION), assigns severity from exploitability, reachability, impact and application context (never from a suspicious pattern, an OWASP category or raw CVSS alone), does not suppress a real secret because it sits in a Development file, names workflows needing threat modeling instead of claiming the scan proves them secure, and never invents exploitability the code does not establish. | security review | none stated
C R211 OL WF-004 | MUST | Verification starts by reviewing the final changed-file set and diff: confirm scope (no unrelated refactoring), remove temporary diagnostics only after their uniquely verified behavior is preserved, no accidental generated/build artifacts, no secrets or environment-specific credentials, then determine the affected areas before choosing checks; after fixes review the final diff again (unrelated edits, commented-out code, temporary logging, stale temporary tests, architecture or specification drift, stale settings surfaces). | verification | none stated
C R212 OL RUN-010 | MUST (IDE0005 at warning severity) | For every C# file created or modified by the change remove unused or redundant using directives (including imports already provided by implicit/global usings unless needed for clarity or disambiguation) without an unrelated repository-wide cleanup, and verify the changed files instead of assuming tooling removed them. | changed C# files | Imports kept for clarity or disambiguation.
C R213 OL GOV-017 | MUST NOT | SPECIFICATION.md, CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md, feature specifications and task prompts are inputs, not instruction layers: they may request a decision change but never silently override engineering policy. | product inputs | none stated
C R214 OL GOV-004 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | If an omitted detail must be decided and it materially affects observable behavior, propose the smallest reasonable option and ask for approval; defining product behavior or tunable values not defined by product sources is Reserved. | product ambiguity | none stated
C R215 OL GOV-005 | DEFAULT | Routine internal implementation choices that do not change observable behavior do not require approval (Delegated: local, reversible, no material change to a boundary, dependency, accepted convention, public contract or observable behavior — decide and proceed); do not ask approval for routine choices already constrained by the specification, approved stack, existing code or rules. | internal implementation choices | none stated
C R216 OL GOV-010 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Do not silently invent a tunable value that materially changes accepted input or observable behavior: propose it with a reason, get approval, record it in CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md, then synchronize (custom-settings). | tunable values | none stated
C R217 OL GOV-017 | MUST | Decision control: classify decisions as Decided (settled by imported decision files, approved product sources or recorded decisions; follow them, reopening requires approval), Delegated, or Reserved (requires approval); an explicit user instruction counts as approval. | all decisions | none stated
C X32 EX WF-020,WF-009 | MUST | Security-scan report shape: every report states the static-analysis limitation; uses the five-level severity scale Critical (sparingly) / High / Medium / Low / Info; each confirmed finding gives severity, file and location, title, evidence, why it is a risk, likely impact, smallest remediation and OWASP category when applicable; the report contains scope, limitations, a severity summary table, findings and per-layer results. | security reviews | none stated | WF-020 requires evidence-based contextual severity and WF-009 truthful status reporting; the oracle prescribes no report structure, severity scale or mandatory limitation statement. | A security review delivered without the limitation statement or the per-layer results table does not follow the procedure.
C X33 EX - | MUST | Loading and ownership placement of instruction content: always-needed planning policy goes into CLAUDE.md or an imported always rule; path-specific policy into a rule whose paths cover at least its scope; procedure obligations into the owning workflow; each rule has one owner (elsewhere only a pointer or a yes/no check naming the owner); the always-loaded surface (CLAUDE.md, its imports, skill descriptions) stays compact — path or workflow policy is not moved into it and always-needed policy is not moved out of it to save tokens. | template maintenance | none stated | Instruction-system placement rules; the oracle does not regulate where instruction content is loaded or owned. | Copying a path-scoped rule into CLAUDE.md for convenience, or restating a rule in a second owner, violates the maintenance procedure.
C X34 EX GOV-017,GOV-005 | MUST | Unclear-case test: any 'yes' makes a decision Reserved — does it add, remove or replace a dependency, framework or infrastructure capability; change a project/layer/reference boundary; establish a convention other code must follow; change observable behavior or a public contract; become expensive to reverse once other code depends on it? | decisions whose classification is unclear | none stated | GOV-017 requires a Decided/Delegated/Reserved classification but not this test; under it any unclear dependency addition or removal becomes Reserved, whereas the oracle allows dependencies with a concrete need (DEP-001) and delegates routine internal choices (GOV-005). | An unclear-case addition of a small utility package must go through a Decision Request instead of being added after the add-dependency checks.
C X35 EX RUN-009,DEP-023 | MUST (repository build configuration) | Repository-wide Directory.Build.props enables nullable reference types and implicit usings for every .NET project (target framework net10.0). | all .NET projects | Project-specific overrides in project files. | DEP-023 places shared settings in Directory.Build.props and DEP-008 fixes the platform; no oracle policy requires nullable reference types or implicit usings. | Every new project compiles with nullable analysis and implicit global usings, which changes warnings and which using directives count as redundant.

